# CVEs we have explicitly accepted in CI. New CVEs (not on this list) fail
# the build — see .github/workflows/test.yml `cve-scan` job.
#
# Format: one GHSA ID per line, optionally with a "# reason" trailing comment.
# pip-audit reads this via --ignore-vuln $(...) — empty lines and #-comments
# are stripped by the workflow.
#
# Each accepted CVE MUST have:
#   - file:line of the relevant code (so the next reviewer can re-check),
#   - a sentence on why it doesn't apply to our deployment,
#   - a target release / date for re-evaluation.

# ---- pypdf 5.1.0 — DoS family via crafted PDFs ----
# Threat model: PDF parsing only happens on (a) admin upload via
# backend/admin.py:upload_document and (b) the offline ingest CLI. Both are
# operator-trusted entrypoints. Resource caps in admin.py:_parse_payload
# (MAX_PDF_PAGES=500, MAX_PDF_TEXT_CHARS=5_000_000) bound the impact of
# a malicious PDF to ~5 MB of extracted text + 500 pages walked. A bump
# to pypdf 6.x is a major version with parsing-behaviour changes — needs a
# regression pass against the existing /docs corpus before shipping.
# Re-evaluate: 2026-08 (after pypdf 6.x has been out a few months and we
# can budget the regression test).
